# The gate's cpu-spinners row and the GUI form of INV-0269-1 (TASK-26 Q7;
# ADR-0264, ADR-0269, ADR-0268 point 3; INV-0264-3's GUI half). Coordinates
# as tests/gui/limits.script's (logical, 1024 x 768, scale 1).
#
# 1. INV-0269-1: a terminal launched from the dock in room `project` and the
#    first terminal's shell, which enters the same room, run in ONE job: the
#    room's `--procs 5` limit counts the processes of both.
# 2. Two rooms with `--cpu 25%` run two spinners each (the rooms' own programs,
#    from the system image); the key latency of a terminal in `home` is
#    measured by the runner's `latency` step and bounded by 300 ms over one
#    screendump read. The kernel's own 50 ms bound for an uncapped process next
#    to capped rooms that spin and burst is checked by t_cpu (make test-qemu).
serial init: gui: gpu on its own page
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen ~> _
type mkdir project\r
screen ~> _
type mkdir other\r
screen ~> _
type room new project --cpu 25% --procs 5 +w ~/project\r
screen project --colour 1 --cpu 25% --procs 5 +w ~/project
screen ~> _
# The dock's chip enters the room; System+Enter launches a terminal in it.
clickc 2f7f8f 300 719 600 7
chord meta ret
origin 105 138
screen Type help to begin, or help tour.
screen project ~/project> _
click 400 120
type sleep 60 &\r
screen [1] sleep 60
screen project ~/project> _
type sleep 60 &\r
screen [2] sleep 60
screen project ~/project> _
# The first terminal's shell enters the same room: its processes go to the
# job the dock's terminal runs in, so the room holds 3 (the dock's shell and
# two sleeps) and two more fit, the third is refused at the one limit.
click 400 80
region 130 76 100 4 f7f7f8
origin 73 106
type room project\r
screen project ~/project> _
type sleep 60 &\r
screen [1] sleep 60
screen project ~/project> _
type sleep 60 &\r
screen [2] sleep 60
screen project ~/project> _
type sleep 60 &\r
prefix hint: room project is at its process limit
screen project ~/project> _
shot one-job
type top\r
prefix project
screen project ~/project> _
type room --leave\r
type cd /\r
screen /> _
# Two rooms at 25% with two spinners each, then the latency of a keystroke in
# home.
type room new spin1 --cpu 25% --procs 6 +w ~/other\r
screen spin1 --colour
screen /> _
type room new spin2 --cpu 25% --procs 6 +w ~/other\r
screen spin2 --colour
screen /> _
type room spin1\r
type spin &\r
screen [1] spin
type spin &\r
screen [2] spin
type room --leave\r
type room spin2\r
type spin &\r
screen [1] spin
type spin &\r
screen [2] spin
type room --leave\r
type cd /\r
pause 1500
latency 10 300
shot spinners
type poweroff\r
exit
